  "goodToKnow": "Die Mietpreisbremse (rent brake) is a German law since 2015: in areas with tight housing markets, rent for a new tenancy may not exceed the ortsübliche Vergleichsmiete (local comparative rent, shown in the Mietspiegel) by more than 10 percent, with exceptions like new builds. It's been extended several times and is controversial, as many landlords ignore it. It has no plural."
